# build output
dist/

# generated types
.astro/

# dependencies
# Both spellings. The trailing slash matches a DIRECTORY only, so a `node_modules`
# SYMLINK — which is how an isolated worktree borrows the main checkout's install, and
# is what every fan-out agent in this repo is told to create instead of installing —
# sails straight past it. One got committed, and CI failed on the next run with
# `ENOTDIR: not a directory, mkdir .../node_modules` during `pnpm install`, which reads
# like a broken runner rather than a stray file in the tree.
node_modules
node_modules/

.netlify/
.idea/

# logs
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# environment variables
#
# A WILDCARD WITH TWO NAMED EXCEPTIONS, and which way round it is stated is the whole change.
# This block used to list three exact names — a list of the files somebody had thought of.
# MEASURED with `git check-ignore`: `.env.development`, `.env.test`, `.env.production.local`,
# `.env.development.local` and `.env.test.local` all fell OUTSIDE it, and those five are not
# invented spellings. They are exactly what Astro and Vite's own `.env.[mode]` and
# `.env.[mode].local` convention produces, so the first person to run a non-default mode makes
# one, and `git status` offers to commit it.
#
# `.env.op`'s HEADER USED TO ARGUE AGAINST THIS WILDCARD, and the argument is answered rather
# than overruled: it said the reference file is what makes the credential path discoverable,
# and a blanket `.env*` would refuse the one file that documents where the credentials live.
# That is right, and `!.env.op` is the answer to it — the file stays addable, by name, where a
# reader can see the exception being made. That header now says so too.
#
# What moved is the DEFAULT. An unlisted `.env` file used to be committed unless somebody had
# named it; it is now ignored unless somebody names it. Only one of those two failure modes
# publishes a secret.
.env*
!.env.op
!.env.example

# local database
.data/

# macOS-specific files
.DS_Store

# agent working files
.scratchpad/
.claude/worktrees/


# python, for dns/ only — octoDNS is the one Python toolchain here
__pycache__/
dns/.venv/

# design-system sync
#
# Syncing this site's palette to a design tool stages that tool's converter into
# `.ds-sync/` and builds its upload directory at `ds-bundle/`. Neither is ours and both
# are regenerated on every sync — the durable half is what sits in `.design-sync/` and is
# NOT listed here: the config pinning which project this repo syncs to, the notes a future
# sync reads first, and the conventions the design agent is handed. `.design-sync/.cache/`
# is machine state, so it goes.
#
# `node_modules` above already covers both directories' installs, in both spellings.
.ds-sync/
ds-bundle/
.design-sync/.cache/
.design-sync/learnings/
